/* book exam traps: Using V·I·t·fs without the ½ doubles the switching loss. The ½ comes from the triangular overlap, not from a duty ratio. | ZVS removes the turn-on overlap, not the conduction loss. The MOSFET still carries current, so I²Ron stays. | ZCS is a turn-off condition. It does not make the switch carry zero current during the on-time, and it does not clamp the off-state voltage to zero. | The tank frequency is 1/(2π√(Lr Cr)), not 1/√(Lr Cr). Missing 2π gives an answer in rad/s. | A resonant converter's gain is not D·Vs. Do not use the buck formula when the control variable is switching frequency. */
